# phase-075 — Teach the language server navigation: goto-definition, references, completion

<!-- GENERATED by rbops/gen-prompts.sh from rbops/phases.json. DO NOT EDIT. -->

| | |
|---|---|
| Severity | `major` |
| Risk | `medium` |
| Depends on | phase-074 |
| Timeout | 120 min |
| Must change | `src/` |

## You must change `src/`

This phase declares `must_touch: [src/]`. The gate fails the phase unless at
least one changed file falls under it. Writing tests, documentation or a report
is not enough — if you finish without touching that area, the phase fails on
exactly that check.


## Evidence — verified finding

```
src/lsp.rs answers questions about a file but cannot move inside it: its public surface is `diagnostics`, `diagnostics_json`, `keyword_pattern`, `escape_json` and `textmate_grammar` (lsp.rs:44-233) — diagnostics plus editor assets, no navigation. Ipp's `lsp/server.py` ships `goto_definition` (:113), `find_references` (:131) and `get_completions` (:149) with enhanced context awareness, because diagnostics without navigation is a linter with a wire protocol: the editor can underline the error but cannot jump to the definition. Phase-017 scaffolded the server; this is the first capability beyond scaffolding.
```

**Re-verify this before you change anything.** If the finding no longer
reproduces on `main`, stop and write that to `FINDINGS.md` — a stale phase must
never be "fixed" by inventing a change.

## Goal

Add goto-definition (name at position to its binding span), find-references (all uses of the binding at position), and completion (keywords + builtins + in-scope names at position) to `src/lsp.rs`, each as a pure function over source text returning JSON the existing `diagnostics_json` shape extends. No server loop changes: capabilities first, transport later.

## Method

1. Read `AGENTS.md` in full. Obey every hard rule; they are not negotiable.
2. Reproduce the finding. Record the exact command and the exact wrong output.
3. Write the failing test FIRST. Watch it fail. Do not touch production code
   until you have a red test that fails for the right reason.
4. Make the smallest change that turns it green.
5. Run the four gates yourself before claiming anything:

   ```bash
   cargo fmt --all -- --check
   cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
   cargo test --all-targets
   ./rbops/verify.sh phase-075
   ```

6. Write `REPORT.md` in the exact shape required by `AGENTS.md` section 4.

## Definition of done

- [ ] goto-definition on a `set` variable's use returns its declaration span (line + column asserted exactly on a fixed fixture — positions are deterministic, never approximate)
- [ ] find-references on one binding returns every use and no use of a same-named binding in another scope (shadowing fixture: inner `x` and outer `x` distinguished)
- [ ] completion at an empty prefix offers keywords, builtins and in-scope session names; completion inside a string literal offers nothing (context awareness asserted, not just prefix matching)
- [ ] all three return the existing `{line, column, ...}` JSON shape extended per capability, and malformed positions (line 0, column past end) are clean errors, never panics
- [ ] edge_* tests cover goto-definition on a builtin (resolves to the builtin registry, not a file span), references to an imported module member (spans the import, not the definition site), completion at EOF without trailing newline, and a 5000-line file (all three answer in under a second — a benchmark assertion, not a wall-time gate)

## Test requirements — non-negotiable

From `AGENTS.md` section 3. Tick each row that applies to this change. For
every row you do NOT cover, write one line in `REPORT.md` saying why.

- [ ] empty — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] singleton — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] boundary — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] out_of_bounds — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] type_mismatch — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] numeric_boundary — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] unicode — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] nesting_recursion — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] duplicate_missing_keys — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] malformed_input — covered / N/A + why
- [ ] resource_limit — covered / N/A + why

You must also:

- at least 3 new `#[test]` functions (or at least 2 new Redblue `test` blocks).
  This is a floor, not a target: it catches "no verification at all". Whether
  your tests COVER the change is judged by the reviewer, and an untested branch
  is a MAJOR finding that sends the phase back.
- at least 1 test named `edge_*`
- at least 1 test that asserts a **failure** is produced, not just a success
- zero new `#[ignore]`, `// skip`, or `allow(clippy::` suppressions
- zero newly-failing pre-existing tests

## Constraints

- Do not touch `.github/workflows/`, `rbops/`, `.opencode/agent/`, or
  `rbops/phases.json`. The gate rejects these paths, and the bot token has no
  `workflows` scope so a push touching `.github/` is refused by GitHub.
- Do not weaken, delete or re-scope any existing test.
- Do not change the language surface listed in `phases/INVARIANTS.md`.
- Keep the diff on-topic. A refactor smuggled into a bug-fix phase is a
  review BLOCKER.
- Do not update README or ROADMAP to claim this works. Update them only when
  the gate is green and you have run the examples yourself.

## If you are blocked

Do not fake progress. Write what you tried, the exact error, and what you
believe is required into `FINDINGS.md`, then stop.

A blocked phase with an honest report is worth more than a green phase with a
lie in it. `verify.sh` will reject the phase anyway; a fabrication only adds a
blocking review finding on top.
